{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/7/codegen_prompts/4.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/7`\n- 题号：`4`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/7/4.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"4\">\n- `description`：将多个面板中的精灵按照其\"朝向\"（由精灵形状的不对称性决定）分组，每组精灵的朝向相同的排成一列输出。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中散布着若干个相同大小（3x3 bbox）的单色精灵，每个精灵的形状在其 3x3 bbox 内是不对称的，具有明确的视觉\"朝向\"（如一个 L 形的开口朝上/下/左/右）。\n  - 精灵使用不同的颜色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个精灵，确定其朝向：将精灵的归一化形状与四个旋转版本比较，朝向由其归一化后所属的旋转类别决定（上、右、下、左）。\n  - 将所有同朝向的精灵分为一组。\n  - 创建输出画布，每组占一列，组内精灵从上到下排列，保持原色，间隔一像素。\n  - 列的顺序为：朝上、朝右、朝下、朝左（从左到右），列之间间隔两像素。\n  - 如果某个朝向没有精灵，则跳过该列。\n\n- `Key insight`：精灵的颜色和位置都是干扰项，唯一的分组键是形状的旋转朝向；解题者需要先抽象出朝向概念，再发现列排列的固定顺序。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/f0f8a26d, train/2601afb7, eval/62593bfd, train/34cfa167, train/e729b7be, train/6165ea8f, train/afe3afe9, train/2ccd9fef\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"f0f8a26d\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3935\nmechanism=0.4682\nlexical=0.0157\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f0f8a26d.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/f0f8a26d.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRotate every foreground bar 90 degrees around its own center on the same canvas.\n\nInput structure\nThe background is the dominant color, and all foreground pixels share one color.\nEach 4-connected foreground object is a solid one-cell-thick horizontal or vertical\nbar with odd length, with single-pixel bars allowed.\n\nRule\nClear the canvas to the background, then redraw every bar with its midpoint, length,\nand color preserved while swapping horizontal and vertical orientation.\n\nKey insight\nThe bars are independent objects: their centers and lengths identify the output\nplacement, so no matching, ordering, or global symmetry is needed.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected monochromatic foreground bars on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"rotate each odd-length horizontal or vertical bar 90 degrees about its midpoint; preserve its color and length, with single-pixel bars unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2601afb7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3742\nmechanism=0.4396\nlexical=0.0163\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/2601afb7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2601afb7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRotate each vertical bar's color one slot right and its height one slot left.\n\nInput structure\n- A dominant background surrounds several monochrome one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Every bar is bottom-aligned and occupies a distinct column.\n- The ordered bar slots are read from left to right.\n\nRule\n- Keep the grid shape and the bar columns unchanged.\n- At slot i, use the color from the previous slot cyclically.\n- At slot i, use the height from the next slot cyclically.\n\nKey insight\n- Color and height are independent cyclic attributes of the ordered bar slots:\n  colors rotate right while heights rotate left.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars ordered left-to-right\",\n  \"transform\": \"redraw each bar in the same column with the previous bar's color cyclically and the next bar's height cyclically\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"62593bfd\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3542\nmechanism=0.4282\nlexical=0.0151\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/62593bfd.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/62593bfd.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSort objects to top or bottom edge by whether their shape (up to rotation/flip) is shared.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Several multicolor connected components (8-connected) scattered across the grid.\n\nRule:\n- Compute each object's canonical shape (binary mask, invariant to rotation and flip).\n- Objects whose shape appears in two or more components → translate to TOP edge (row 0).\n- Objects whose shape is unique → translate to BOTTOM edge (row H−h).\n- Horizontal position (left column) is preserved; only vertical translation changes.\n\nKey insight: The sorting criterion is shape frequency (rotation-invariant), not area — duplicated shapes go up, unique shapes go down.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"all connected components (objects) on the background\",\n  \"dst\": \"translate each object d vertically to an edge (x preserved)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"group objects by their pixel-count (area). If an area value occurs >=2 times, those objects go to the TOP edge; if the area is unique, that object goes to the BOTTOM edge\",\n  \"transform\": \"duplicated-size -> top; singleton-size -> bottom\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"34cfa167\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3249\nmechanism=0.4028\nlexical=0.0149\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, operation:reflect, operation:sort_order, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/34cfa167.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/34cfa167.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete a four-corner framed rectangle from one decorated anchor rectangle and its diagonal mate.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Two same-color solid rectangular anchors of the same size sit on opposite\n  diagonal corners, with the first anchor above-left of the second.\n- The upper-left anchor has two one-cell-thick vertical control bars to its\n  right and two one-cell-thick horizontal control bars below it.\n\nRule:\n- Copy the anchor rectangle into the two missing corners of the implied\n  larger rectangle.\n- Repeat the right-side control bars horizontally between the left and right\n  anchors, using their spacing as the period, and draw the outer top and\n  bottom borders in the first right-control color.\n- Repeat the below-side control bars vertically between the top and bottom\n  anchors, using the same period, and draw the outer left and right borders\n  in the first below-control color.\n\nKey insight: The small control bars are the first two ticks of two periodic\nframe patterns; the diagonal anchor supplies the opposite corner and the\nmissing two anchor copies.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"two same-color solid rectangular anchors, with two right control bars and two below control bars beside the upper-left anchor\",\n  \"dst\": \"the missing two anchor corners and periodic frame segments between all four anchors\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy the anchor rectangle into the missing corners; repeat the right-control colors across the top and bottom anchor rows and outer borders, and repeat the below-control colors down the left and right side bars using the same spacing\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e729b7be\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3179\nmechanism=0.3924\nlexical=0.0152\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e729b7be.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e729b7be.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete the scene by adding the point-reflected copy of the colored object across the central marker.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has odd dimensions, a dominant background, and a center-row marker color appearing only at the left edge, center, and right edge.\n- A single divider color fills the center column except for the center marker.\n- All remaining foreground pixels form the object to copy, entirely on the left side of the divider.\nRule\n- Keep the input unchanged.\n- For every object pixel, paint the pixel rotated 180 degrees around the center marker with the same color.\nKey insight\n- The center marker is the rotation center; the yellow-looking divider is not mirrored, it only separates the source from the empty target side.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"colored foreground object pixels excluding the center-column divider and center-row markers\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy each source pixel to its 180-degree point-reflection through the center marker, preserving the original pixels, divider, and markers\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6165ea8f\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3421\nmechanism=0.4107\nlexical=0.0142\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:reflect, operation:rotate, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6165ea8f.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6165ea8f.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nBuild a color-labeled shape-equivalence table from the objects listed on the right edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background contains one main 4-connected object for each foreground color.\n- The rightmost column has one singleton pixel of each foreground color, listed top-to-bottom.\n- Those singleton pixels define the row and column order of the output table.\n\nRule:\n- Normalize each main object to its tight mask and compare masks up to rotation or reflection.\n- Draw 2x2 color labels across the top and down the left, separated by one background row/column.\n- For each off-diagonal table cell, paint a 2x2 red block when the two labeled objects have the same shape under rotation/reflection, otherwise paint a 2x2 grey block.\n- Leave diagonal cells and all separators as background.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object positions and original orientations are distractors; the relation is dihedral shape equivalence, while the right-edge legend fixes the table order.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"main colored objects plus right-edge singleton color legend\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"实施方案：\n\n1. `main()` 用 4 连通对象提取每个精灵，裁成 tight bbox，基于四个旋转的字典序规范形态求唯一旋转索引，把它映射到 `up/right/down/left` 四类，再按读序稳定分组。\n2. `generate_input()` 先预计算所有合法的 3x3 朝向精灵族（full bbox、4 连通、四向旋转全不同），随机选若干族和朝向，随机散布到输入画布，颜色唯一，朝向子集和组大小都变化。\n3. 写入目标文件后按给定 100 次自检和 `py_compile` 运行；如果有失败，直接回修生成器或朝向判定，再清掉 `__pycache__`。"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport numpy as np\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef mask_from_bits(bits):\n    arr = np.zeros((3,3), dtype=bool)\n    for i in range(9):\n        if bits >> i & 1:\n            arr[i//3, i%3] = True\n    return arr\n\ndef full_bbox(m):\n    return all(m[r,:].any() for r in range(3)) and all(m[:,c].any() for c in range(3))\n\ndef connected(m):\n    pts = list(map(tuple, np.argwhere(m)))\n    if not pts:\n        return False\n    seen = {pts[0]}\n    stack = [pts[0]]\n    while stack:\n        r,c = stack.pop()\n        for dr,dc in ((1,0),(-1,0),(0,1),(0,-1)):\n            nr,nc = r+dr,c+dc\n            if 0<=nr<3 and 0<=nc<3 and m[nr,nc] and (nr,nc) not in seen:\n                seen.add((nr,nc))\n                stack.append((nr,nc))\n    return len(seen)==len(pts)\n\ndef key(m):\n    return tuple(''.join('1' if x else '0' for x in row) for row in m)\n\nfamilies=[]\nareas=Counter()\nfor bits in range(1,1<<9):\n    m=mask_from_bits(bits)\n    if not full_bbox(m) or not connected(m):\n        continue\n    variants=[np.rot90(m,k) for k in range(4)]\n    keys=[key(v) for v in variants]\n    if len(set(keys))<4:\n        continue\n    mk=min(keys)\n    if keys[0]==mk:\n        families.append(m)\n        areas[int(m.sum())]+=1\nprint('families',len(families),'areas',areas)\nfor m in families[:20]:\n    print('---')\n    for row in m.astype(int):\n        print(''.join(map(str,row)))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport numpy as np\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef mask_from_bits(bits):\n    arr = np.zeros((3,3), dtype=bool)\n    for i in range(9):\n        if bits >> i & 1:\n            arr[i//3, i%3] = True\n    return arr\n\ndef full_bbox(m):\n    return all(m[r,:].any() for r in range(3)) and all(m[:,c].any() for c in range(3))\n\ndef connected(m):\n    pts = list(map(tuple, np.argwhere(m)))\n    if not pts:\n        return False\n    seen = {pts[0]}\n    stack = [pts[0]]\n    while stack:\n        r,c = stack.pop()\n        for dr,dc in ((1,0),(-1,0),(0,1),(0,-1)):\n            nr,nc = r+dr,c+dc\n            if 0<=nr<3 and 0<=nc<3 and m[nr,nc] and (nr,nc) not in seen:\n                seen.add((nr,nc))\n                stack.append((nr,nc))\n    return len(seen)==len(pts)\n\ndef key(m):\n    return tuple(''.join('1' if x else '0' for x in row) for row in m)\n\nfamilies=[]\nareas=Counter()\nfor bits in range(1,1<<9):\n    m=mask_from_bits(bits)\n    if not full_bbox(m) or not connected(m):\n        continue\n    variants=[np.rot90(m,k) for k in range(4)]\n    keys=[key(v) for v in variants]\n    if len(set(keys))<4:\n        continue\n    mk=min(keys)\n    if keys[0]==mk:\n        families.append(m)\n        areas[int(m.sum())]+=1\nprint('families',len(families),'areas',areas)\nfor m in families[:20]:\n    print('---')\n    for row in m.astype(int):\n        print(''.join(map(str,row)))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"families 25 areas Counter({6: 11, 7: 7, 5: 5, 8: 2})\n---\n001\n111\n010\n---\n010\n011\n110\n---\n001\n011\n110\n---\n011\n011\n110\n---\n001\n111\n110\n---\n001\n111\n001\n---\n010\n111\n101\n---\n001\n111\n101\n---\n011\n111\n101\n---\n010\n111\n011\n---\n001\n111\n011\n---\n011\n010\n111\n---\n011\n110\n111\n---\n001\n001\n111\n---\n011\n001\n111\n---\n001\n101\n111\n---\n101\n101\n111\n---\n011\n101\n111\n---\n010\n011\n111\n---\n001\n011\n111\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef mask_from_bits(bits):\n    arr = np.zeros((3,3), dtype=bool)\n    for i in range(9):\n        if bits >> i & 1:\n            arr[i//3, i%3] = True\n    return arr\n\ndef full_bbox(m):\n    return all(m[r,:].any() for r in range(3)) and all(m[:,c].any() for c in range(3))\n\ndef connected(m):\n    pts = list(map(tuple, np.argwhere(m)))\n    if not pts:\n        return False\n    seen = {pts[0]}\n    stack = [pts[0]]\n    while stack:\n        r,c = stack.pop()\n        for dr,dc in ((1,0),(-1,0),(0,1),(0,-1)):\n            nr,nc = r+dr,c+dc\n            if 0<=nr<3 and 0<=nc<3 and m[nr,nc] and (nr,nc) not in seen:\n                seen.add((nr,nc))\n                stack.append((nr,nc))\n    return len(seen)==len(pts)\n\ndef key(m):\n    return tuple(''.join('1' if x else '0' for x in row) for row in m)\n\nfamilies=[]\nfor bits in range(1,1<<9):\n    m=mask_from_bits(bits)\n    if not full_bbox(m) or not connected(m):\n        continue\n    variants=[np.rot90(m,k) for k in range(4)]\n    keys=[key(v) for v in variants]\n    if len(set(keys))<4:\n        continue\n    mk=min(keys)\n    if keys[0]==mk and 5 <= int(m.sum()) <= 7:\n        families.append(m)\nprint('families',len(families))\nfor idx,m in enumerate(families):\n    print('idx',idx,'area',int(m.sum()))\n    for row in m.astype(int):\n        print(''.join(map(str,row)))\n    print()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef mask_from_bits(bits):\n    arr = np.zeros((3,3), dtype=bool)\n    for i in range(9):\n        if bits >> i & 1:\n            arr[i//3, i%3] = True\n    return arr\n\ndef full_bbox(m):\n    return all(m[r,:].any() for r in range(3)) and all(m[:,c].any() for c in range(3))\n\ndef connected(m):\n    pts = list(map(tuple, np.argwhere(m)))\n    if not pts:\n        return False\n    seen = {pts[0]}\n    stack = [pts[0]]\n    while stack:\n        r,c = stack.pop()\n        for dr,dc in ((1,0),(-1,0),(0,1),(0,-1)):\n            nr,nc = r+dr,c+dc\n            if 0<=nr<3 and 0<=nc<3 and m[nr,nc] and (nr,nc) not in seen:\n                seen.add((nr,nc))\n                stack.append((nr,nc))\n    return len(seen)==len(pts)\n\ndef key(m):\n    return tuple(''.join('1' if x else '0' for x in row) for row in m)\n\nfamilies=[]\nfor bits in range(1,1<<9):\n    m=mask_from_bits(bits)\n    if not full_bbox(m) or not connected(m):\n        continue\n    variants=[np.rot90(m,k) for k in range(4)]\n    keys=[key(v) for v in variants]\n    if len(set(keys))<4:\n        continue\n    mk=min(keys)\n    if keys[0]==mk and 5 <= int(m.sum()) <= 7:\n        families.append(m)\nprint('families',len(families))\nfor idx,m in enumerate(families):\n    print('idx',idx,'area',int(m.sum()))\n    for row in m.astype(int):\n        print(''.join(map(str,row)))\n    print()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"families 23\nidx 0 area 5\n001\n111\n010\n\nidx 1 area 5\n010\n011\n110\n\nidx 2 area 5\n001\n011\n110\n\nidx 3 area 6\n011\n011\n110\n\nidx 4 area 6\n001\n111\n110\n\nidx 5 area 5\n001\n111\n001\n\nidx 6 area 6\n010\n111\n101\n\nidx 7 area 6\n001\n111\n101\n\nidx 8 area 7\n011\n111\n101\n\nidx 9 area 6\n010\n111\n011\n\nidx 10 area 6\n001\n111\n011\n\nidx 11 area 6\n011\n010\n111\n\nidx 12 area 7\n011\n110\n111\n\nidx 13 area 5\n001\n001\n111\n\nidx 14 area 6